# Allowed failures of the Air passes' oracles
# (tests/differential/air_passes.zig, `zig build diff-air-passes`).
# One line: <oracle> <kind> <reason>. Oracles and kinds: float (interval,
# finite, slice, violation), legalize (bits), setup (invariant), held (pruned).
# A line whose oracle never fails in that kind fails the run (an unexpected
# pass); a failure no line names fails it too. Empty: every oracle is clean.
float finite the merged Float's overflow contract: `+ - * /` on finite operands called finite (1e300 * 1e300 is inf)
float interval the merged Float takes an unranged parameter NaN-free: a comparison on a NaN parameter is decided as if it were a number
